### collections_records-create

File a new row.

Add a record to a collection.

The declared hooks normalise the data first, then it is validated against the
schema and, for a field declared unique, against what is already stored.

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "collection": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Id of the collection to file the record into."
    },
    "data": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "The record's fields, as declared by its collection's schema.",
      "additionalProperties": true
    },
    "content": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "The Markdown body, for a collection of format md. Ignored for json."
    },
    "_reasoning": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "MANDATORY. NEVER FORGET. Explain why this specific tool is being called now, what outcome you expect, and the immediate next step if that helps clarify the call. Do not leave this empty.",
      "minLength": 1
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "collection",
    "data",
    "_reasoning"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

